From 004940b58f73ccf128275694fbfc48b94f90a46d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObliviOS Build <build@oblivios.local>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 15:32:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] compartments: parse the place and cell data without a regex
 and read the cells under their own lock

From: beau4201 <beau.ten.berge@gmail.com>

The first read of cells.tsv (400,000 lines) ran under the ActivityManager lock on lynx
2026110101 and blocked it for 15 s or more: personaFor waited in operatorOf for
mPlacesLock, held by the background thread that parsed the file with one regex per field.

CellSubset and Places are parsed in one pass over the characters with the same strict
grammar, no regex and no split; the coordinates are computed by one correctly rounded
division. The cells have their own lock, so a caller that needs only the places never waits
for the cell parse.
